      "og_image": "https://codeberg.org/mv12star/shitter/-/summary-card",
      "groq_label": "Nitter instances multiplied beyond pre-takedown levels by using bulk account markets and residential proxies to bypass Twitter's login enforcement.",
      "groq_discussion": "Discussion type: – Balanced:\n\nThis project aims to solve the problem of accessing Twitter content without requiring a user account or using the platform's native interface. The Hacker News discussion was generally mixed, with many commenters appreciating its clean user interface and the project's approach to bypassing forced login barriers. At the same time, several commenters raised concerns about instance longevity and rate limits, arguing that public instances will inevitably shut down over time and result in broken links. Overall, the discussion suggests that the community sees promise in the project but believes there are important challenges that still need to be addressed.",
